        "articleNumber": "4118184",
        "articleTitle": "Case Study 2: HADRIAN: A Human Factors Computer-Aided Inclusive Design Tool for Transport Planning",
        "volume": null,
        "issue": null,
        "startPage": "45",
        "endPage": "60",
        "publisher": "IET",
        "articleContentType": "Conferences",
        "publicationTitle": "The Institution of Engineering and Technology Seminar on Railway Human Factors in a Changing World",
        "authors": [
            {
                "id": null,
                "preferredName": "Steve Summerskill",
                "firstName": "Steve",
                "lastName": "Summerskill"
            },
            {
                "id": null,
                "preferredName": "Ruth Sims",
                "firstName": "Ruth",
                "lastName": "Sims"
            },
            {
                "id": null,
                "preferredName": "Diane Gyi",
                "firstName": "Diane",
                "lastName": "Gyi"
            },
            {
                "id": null,
                "preferredName": "Keith Case",
                "firstName": "Keith",
                "lastName": "Case"
            },
            {
                "id": null,
                "preferredName": "Russ Marshall",
                "firstName": "Russ",
                "lastName": "Marshall"
            },
            {
                "id": null,
                "preferredName": "Mark Porter",
                "firstName": "Mark",
                "lastName": "Porter"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "HADRIAN is a computer-based inclusive design tool developed initially to support the design of kitchen and shopping based tasks. The tool is currently being expanded to include data on an individual's ability to undertake a variety of transport-related tasks, such as vehicle ingress/egress, coping with uneven surfaces, steps, street furniture and complex pedestrian environments. A feature of the enhanced HADRIAN tool will be a journey planner that compares an individual's physical, cognitive and emotional abilities with the demands that will be placed upon that individual depending on the mode(s) of transport available and the route options",
